import{_ as t,o as n,c as a,a2 as i}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 458 | Dragon Ball · Law-First Comparison: How Heng Yuan Zhou Avoids Combat-Power Inflation","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 458 | Dragon Ball · Law-First Comparison: How Heng Yuan Zhou Avoids Combat-Power Inflation","no":458,"module":2,"tags":["Myriad-Realms Benchmark","Dragon Ball","Law-First Axiom","Combat-Power Inflation","Comparison","Never Retcon"],"related":["40-Symbiotic Constitution General Outline","27-Anchor Calibration and Maintenance","14-Unified Cultivation Realm Classification"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0458_模块2-龙珠-法则优先对照-衡元宙如何避免战力膨胀.md","filePath":"en/0458_模块2-龙珠-法则优先对照-衡元宙如何避免战力膨胀.md"}'),o={name:"en/0458_模块2-龙珠-法则优先对照-衡元宙如何避免战力膨胀.md"};function s(r,e,l,d,u,c){return n(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[i('<h1 id="entry-458-dragon-ball-·-law-first-comparison-how-heng-yuan-zhou-avoids-combat-power-inflation" tabindex="-1">Entry 458 | Dragon Ball · Law-First Comparison: How Heng Yuan Zhou Avoids Combat-Power Inflation <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-458-dragon-ball-·-law-first-comparison-how-heng-yuan-zhou-avoids-combat-power-inflation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 458 | Dragon Ball · Law-First Comparison: How Heng Yuan Zhou Avoids Combat-Power Inflation&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Dragon Ball Full Decomposition (Entry 27 · Alternative 7) | Benchmark base: Documents 40, 27, 14</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-why-heng-yuan-zhou-will-not-become-the-next-dragon-ball" tabindex="-1">Introduction: why Heng Yuan Zhou will not become the next Dragon Ball <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-why-heng-yuan-zhou-will-not-become-the-next-dragon-ball" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: why Heng Yuan Zhou will not become the next Dragon Ball&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dragon Ball&#39;s combat-power inflation root cause is law not preceding — plot needs who strong, law lets who strong. Why will Heng Yuan Zhou not repeat the mistake? The answer is the <strong>law-first axiom</strong>: law precedes, never retcons, never ends abruptly; setting self-consistency above plot convenience; plot must not kidnap setting; worldview can infinitely expand without collapse. This entry takes the law-first axiom as core, comparing item by item Dragon Ball and Heng Yuan Zhou on &quot;how to avoid combat-power inflation.&quot;</p><p>This entry&#39;s judging base is the six top-level axioms and five mandatory cores, with the law-first axiom as core. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones-dragon-ball-s-disease-cause" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones (Dragon Ball&#39;s Disease Cause) <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones-dragon-ball-s-disease-cause" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones (Dragon Ball&#39;s Disease Cause)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dragon Ball combat-power inflation&#39;s disease cause:</p><ul><li><strong>Law legislated late</strong>: plot need first, then patch setting explanation — &quot;why did Goku suddenly become Super Saiyan God? Because of the ritual&quot;</li><li><strong>Expansion by overturning</strong>: new transformation, new universe, new tier, all overturn old setting</li><li><strong>Plot kidnaps setting</strong>: can&#39;t win then temporarily add a transformation layer; law gives way anytime</li><li><strong>Conclusion</strong>: law not preceding = combat power inevitably inflates</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-dragon-ball-s-result" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Dragon Ball&#39;s Result) <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-dragon-ball-s-result" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Dragon Ball&#39;s Result)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>How law not preceding feeds historical regression:</p><ol><li><strong>Reader trust collapses</strong>: when readers find law can be broken anytime, worldview credibility zeroed</li><li><strong>Knowledge not accumulated</strong>: early setting invalidated late; civilization cannot settle cultivation experience</li><li><strong>History discontinuous</strong>: because setting changes anytime, worldview&#39;s historical feel reset repeatedly</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking-dragon-ball-s-beneficiary" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking (Dragon Ball&#39;s Beneficiary) <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking-dragon-ball-s-beneficiary" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking (Dragon Ball&#39;s Beneficiary)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Law not preceding&#39;s sole beneficiary is Goku: all laws give way for him to win. He does not need to obey &quot;breakthrough needs cultivation duration&quot; law, because anger can transform; he does not need to obey &quot;revival has price&quot; law, because wishing can restore. <strong>Law not preceding = institutional protective umbrella for protagonist&#39;s predatory thinking.</strong></p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative-heng-yuan-zhou-s-answer" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative (Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Answer) <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative-heng-yuan-zhou-s-answer" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative (Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Answer)&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dragon Ball Law Late</th><th>Heng Yuan Zhou Law First</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Plot first then patch setting</td><td>Law-first axiom: legislate first then expand</td></tr><tr><td>Expansion by overturning old setting</td><td>New dimensions (Multiverse, Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse) via appendix increment</td></tr><tr><td>Plot kidnaps setting</td><td>Setting self-consistency above plot convenience; plot must not kidnap setting</td></tr><tr><td>Emotion = breakthrough key</td><td>Nine-realm promotion triple conditions: cultivation duration + mind-cultivation exam + contribution points</td></tr><tr><td>Revival rules change with plot</td><td>Causal self-discipline axiom: revival goes Symbiotic Court approval; whole process trailed</td></tr><tr><td>Combat-power inflation</td><td>Anchor calibration (Doc 027) periodically calibrates energy definitions</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: Quest Sediment Domain replicates Dragon Ball world; inject law-first axiom</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: compare every Dragon Ball &quot;temporary transformation,&quot; &quot;temporary revival,&quot; &quot;temporary universe addition&quot; against Heng Yuan Zhou law; observe which still hold</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: count &quot;law-giving-way times,&quot; &quot;appendix-increment times,&quot; &quot;plot-kidnapping times&quot;</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: output <em>Law-First Injecting Dragon Ball World Benefit Report</em>, quantifying &quot;legislate first then expand&quot; effect on stamping out combat-power inflation</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Dragon Ball self-consistency: 2/10</strong> (law late = numerical inflation + multi-line retcon)</li><li><strong>Heng Yuan Zhou self-consistency: 9.5/10</strong> (law precedes + appendix increment + anchor calibration)</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk</strong>: Dragon Ball = extremely high, Heng Yuan Zhou = extremely low</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency</strong>: Dragon Ball = high, Heng Yuan Zhou = extremely low (network)</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: law preceding makes early setting not invalidated late; energy investment not wasted</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: law does not give way to protagonist; Goku cannot break through by anger</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo at least self-consistent within one book; Dragon Ball needs law-first to be self-consistent</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: law equal to all Myriad Ranks; no exception for protagonist</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: law preceding = can infinitely expand without collapse; this is Heng Yuan Zhou and Dragon Ball&#39;s ultimate divide</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power inherent in all; easygoing retain guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin eliminates predation motive</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dragon Ball&#39;s combat-power inflation is not Toriyama alone&#39;s fault, but &quot;law legislated late&quot; structural disease&#39;s inevitable result. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s answer is the law-first axiom: legislate first, then expand, never retcon, never end abruptly. Let plot adapt to law, not let law accommodate plot — this one sentence is the lesson Dragon Ball exchanged for with forty years of blood and tears.</p><p>One more layer: Dragon Ball&#39;s numerical inflation has a hidden accelerator — reader expectation. When readers see SSJ1 is cool, they want to see SSJ2; see SSJ2 is cool, they want to see SSJ3. Commercial logic requires &quot;stronger than last time,&quot; so law has to give way again and again. The reason Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s law-first axiom can avoid this trap is it wrote &quot;expansion via appendix&quot; into the constitution from the start — adding a new realm does not overturn old setting, but accesses as an appendix increment. This means readers will never see the embarrassment of &quot;early numbers invalidated,&quot; because law itself promises &quot;old setting always valid.&quot; This is the institution&#39;s constraint on human nature (including commercial logic).</p><p>In the final analysis, Dragon Ball · law-first comparison · how Heng Yuan Zhou avoids combat-power inflation described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./457_模块2-龙珠-万族共和方案-打破人族赛亚人本位.html">Entry 457 · Myriad-Ranks Republicanism</a> · <a href="./436_模块2-龙珠-战力膨胀批判-从几百到无穷的设定崩坏.html">Entry 436 · Combat-Power Inflation</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/40-共生宪法总纲.html">40-Symbiotic Constitution General Outline</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',28)])])}const m=t(o,[["render",s]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
